<font class="content">Posted On 2002-03-11 14:04:00 by <a href="http://">Charoth</a></td></tr></table></td></tr></table><br>The Caller in Fungus Grove was calling us out Saturday, saying things like "You can't do this on easy mode!" and "You're down faster then a .." well, you get the idea. So we got 2 groups up, and started out the quest on easy, then harder and finally the hardest, and it was still kind of boring and not enough killing. So we had the idea of starting up two different callers at the same time and fighting upwards of 6+ mobs at anyone time (more if we killed slow).<BR><BR>Nothing like calling out what mobs are alive, what mobs are dead, where they are, and having 18 people running all over the place to make them dead ;)  Fun stuff indeeed, we didn't get the patch tunic thing we wanted, but I think everyone had a fun time. I know I did.<br /><br />Next stop was the General in Echo, swift kill, and another sword. Then we headed down to CT to see what the new breed of leeezards were up to. We figured we'd try the archon temple, made it to the base of it, got wiped out learning the brown lizards are the tough lizards :) Picked up, started over and and made our way up the temple, inch by inch, level by level until we reached the top. Hoping for something interesting, and all we find is a rooted, green con mob with a Gazillion HP. So we hit it for a while, found out its a quest mob of some sort then decided we'd make our way down.<br /><br />Funny aggro on the temple top, wipe out number 2, pick up try again, figuring we could lev invis off the top. Weird aggro again, coffin time for wipe number 3 to end out the day. ;)</td></tr></table></td></tr></table><br>


